# Instrumented directly: renamingThreadId correctly becomes the target
# thread id immediately, then reverts to null one requestAnimationFrame
# later, with domInputCount:2 observed in between — root cause found (see
# acceptance.md): two simultaneously-rendered rename <input> instances
# (sidebar row + title bar, since this is the ACTIVE thread) each schedule
# their own setTimeout(() => input.focus()); the second to fire steals
# focus from the first, firing a genuine (not involuntary-removal) blur
# that commits/closes the rename.

# Confirmed renaming a NON-active thread (single instance) works fine —
# isolates the defect to the dual-render case.

# --- Fix applied: _renameAutoFocusClaimedForThreadId (app.js) ---

